-- title:
--   Étaleness of the ∞-cusp chart at first-reduction places
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that becomes trivial in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, and $j$ lying in the level-one $q$-expansion field over $\mathbb{Q}$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, with algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ compatible with $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; let $pb$ be a unit of $\mathbb{Z}/(M/p)$ represented by $p$, and $\delta$ the permutation of places of $\bar F =$ `Fbar p M H hpM κ` induced, through `SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut`, by the diamond automorphism attached to a $\Gamma_0(M/p)$-lift of $pb$. Let $\theta$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphism of $F_M =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` inducing, via `hwgen`, the action of $\mathfrak{X}.w$ on points of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$, and let $\alpha : F_{M/p} \to F_M$ be a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map that is the identity on underlying Laurent series, with $\alpha$ and $\theta \circ \alpha$ integral. Further data: a place specialisation $\mathrm{Psp}$, a prolongation datum $\mathrm{Rpd} = (R_1,R_2)$ for $(\mathrm{Psp},\theta)$, the hypothesis that on elements $\alpha v$ integral for both prolongations the $R_2$-residue is the $p$-power $q$-expansion Frobenius of the $R_1$-residue, and a compatibility hypothesis `hcomp` identifying, for $i \in \{0,1\}$, the place of a closed point of the fibre model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ above a given point with $\mathrm{Psp}.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\alpha$ respectively $\delta \circ \mathrm{Psp}.\mathrm{reduceSnd}\,(\theta \circ \alpha)$ of that point. Let $v$ be a place of $\bar F$ over $\kappa$ of the form $\mathrm{reduceFst}\,\alpha\,(c)$ with $c$ on the $\infty$-side, let $x' \in F_{M/p}$ have $q$-expansion $j$ and $t \in F_M$ have $q$-expansion $j(q^p) \cdot j^{-p}$. Then the set $S = \alpha(\mathrm{integralOverPoleChart}\,A\,x') \cup \{t - a : a \in A\}$ satisfies `Rpd.ChartEtaleAt α v S`: there are $z \in S$ and a monic $m \in F_{M/p}[Y]$ of degree $p+1$ such that $z$ is $R_2$-integral with $R_2$-residue whose Laurent expansion has a non-zero coefficient in some degree prime to $p$, the field generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by $\alpha(F_{M/p}) \cup \{z\}$ is all of $F_M$, $z$ is a root of $m^{\alpha}$, every $\alpha(m_i)$ lies in the subring generated by $S$, and whenever $(m^{\alpha})'(z)$ is $R_1$-integral its $R_1$-residue does not have value $0$ at $v$.
--
--   This supplies the étale-generator clause for the chart around an $\infty$-side cusp in the reduction modulo $p$ of $X_H(M)$: the cusp coordinate $t_\infty = j(q^p)/j^p$ is a generator of $F_M$ over $\alpha(F_{M/p})$ satisfying the Kronecker-model equation of degree $p+1$, and the derivative is non-vanishing at the place under consideration. It is used by [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isCuspChartFstAt_of_isInftySide_prolongationDatum`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_isCuspChartFstAt_of_isInftySide_prolongationDatum) in the analysis of the two components of the fibre at $p$.
